Package: TEVRA
Title: Computes and Maps AIRR Features onto Transcriptionally Defined Neighbourhoods
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Grace", "Hattersley", , "gracehattersley@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: TEVRA takes as input paired scRNA-seq and scBCR/TCR-seq data after
    standard preprocessing. Transcriptional neighbourhoods can be defined via 
    Leiden clustering of a k-nearest-neighbour graph, or the 
    user can supply assignments obtained from established methods (Milo, 
    metacell etc). For each neighbourhood, TEVRA computes repertoire features 
    including receptor recovery, clonal expansion and diversity, CDR3-receptor 
    convergence and, for B cells, SHM and isotype composition, including 
    appropriate normalisation for neighbourhood size, sampling depth and CDR3 
    sequence length, where relevant. Computed features are then assigned back 
    onto neighbourhoods for visualisation and downstream analysis.
